Fixed. All 15 tests pass and typecheck is clean.

**The bug:** `src/resources/storage.ts:25` — `clampToStorageCap` clamped `wood` and `stone` to `Math.min(resource, cap)` but returned `food` untouched, so food accumulated without limit while every other resource was capped at the same `storageCap`.

**The fix:** clamp `food` the same way — `food: Math.min(resources.food, cap)`. Also updated the two now-stale comments (the function docstring's "BUG" note and the `utilizationOf` note referencing the "still-buggy food case").

`clampToStorageCap` is the single choke point that `advanceTurn` calls for every resource after production, so capping food there fixes every resource consistently. No test changes were needed.


